    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0246" n="234" xml:id="pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/1278: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-08T19:00:00+03:00">February 8, 1943—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. My 68, January 31, 3 p.m. from Moscow and 112 of February 6, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="82" xml:id="d156-f1"/> The Czechoslovak Ambassador, who is often
                    considered here to be a mouthpiece of the Soviet Government, has stated that
                    there is much talk in Kuibyshev with regard to the possibility of Finland’s
                    withdrawal from the war, that in December Molotov had questioned him on the
                    subject and had appeared very interested in it. He spoke of the possible
                    conditions of such a withdrawal and said that any peace overtures would have to
                    come from a third power. When asked what power he had in mind he replied the
                    United States or Sweden. I am not sure that the Ambassador, who called by
                    appointment, was expressing merely personal views or those reflecting those of
                    the Soviet Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
